\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb98\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri758\sl244\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The performance summary\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in the upper right\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 corner of Figure 4.16 shows peaks of 128 ft\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 lbs and 119 HP.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These are very\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 close to the factory ratings of 127 ft lbs and 130 HP, especially considering you knew almost nothing about the engine.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These results would probably be close enough for you to now make modifications on to see what helps or hurts performance.\expnd13\expndtw65  \expnd0\expndtw0 If some modification showed a 5 HP \f6\b1\i1 gain\f0\b0\i0 , you could be reasonable sure your\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 engine should show about\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a 5 HP \f6\b1\i1 gain\f0\b0\i0 , even though the predicted HP may\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 be about 10 HP low.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery365\footery644\margtsxn740\margbsxn840\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs28\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb129\f0\fs28\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s10\ls34\ilvl0\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li764\fi-404\sl240\slmult1\sb1\tx764\f2\fs28\b1\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Fine\expnd-2\expndtw-9  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Tuning\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri821\sl244\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 The Engine Analyzer\'92s torque is about\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 right, the HP is low and the RPMs where both peak (3000 and 3500 for torque, and 5500 for HP) are lower than the factory rating.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You may not know this now, but most modifications which improve air flow or performance will increase HP more than torque and will shift the peak RPMs to a higher RPM.\expnd16\expndtw80  \expnd0\expndtw0 It looks like some components with \'93improved breathing\'94 would help the program match the factory ratings.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri821\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 You may have noticed when you picked several of the Typical example components, there was a higher performance example available.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 For\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 example,\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 there\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 was\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 a\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Typical\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Stock\expnd0\expndtw-2  \f6\b1\i1\expnd0\expndtw0 HO\expnd0\expndtw-1  \f0\b0\i0\expnd0\expndtw0 OHC\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 cam\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 available\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 instead\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 just\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Typical\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Stock\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 OHC\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 cam.\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Try\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 installing the HO cam and see the effect.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par
