\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\fi-1\ri821\sl244\slmult1\sb236\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Because you will get into more detail in this\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 example, be sure to have selected Experienced User in Preferences at the Main Screen. However,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 keep\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Cam/Valve\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Train\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 menu\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 simple,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 leave\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 \'93Show\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Valve\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Open/Close\'94\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 unchecked.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (See\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Figure\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 4.1\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Example\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 4.1) Then, Open a fresh copy of the 302-4V from the Engine Library by clicking on the Engine Library button at the top of the Main Screen as shown in Example 4.1, Figure 4.2.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri4938\sl244\slmult1\tx5345\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Calculate Performance so the program\'92s History Log has a record of how the stock cam performs.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 At the Test Results screen, click on View (must be in Experienced User mode), then click on Show History Now.\tab You will see the History\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Log appear\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 at\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 bottom\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 of\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 screen as\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 shown in Figure\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 4.23.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 You will notice in the left column, a Test Title which the program has given the test consisting of the Engine name and the time and date of the test.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If you click on any Test Title other than the first one, the program will ask if you want to change the Test Title, or retrieve the specs which produced those test results (Figure 4.22).\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you click\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 on the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Test\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Title\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 top row,\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 it\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 assumes\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 you want\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 to change or edit the Test Title.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Click on the first Test Title and enter a name like \'93Stock \expnd0\expndtw-2 Cam\'94.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb2\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri758\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Click on \'93Don\'92t\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Show History\'94 at\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the top of the History\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 Log screen to close it.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Then, in the lower section of results called the Special Calculations take a look at some results.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 In particular, note Overlap Area, Total Exh/Int % and Vlv Area in the Valve Flow and Cam Calculations section; Dynamic Comp Ratio, Est Idle Vac and Theo. Crank Comprssn in the General Engine Calculations, and Rec Inertial Len in the \'91Starting Point\'92 Suggestions section.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Figure 4.24.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 These have been tabulated in Table 4.2 a couple pages ahead, and will be discussed shortly.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery365\footery644\margtsxn740\margbsxn840\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb90\sa1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li814\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20
