\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb26\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb13\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri821\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 A good analogy of inertia tuning is the "water hammer" effect in old plumbing when you quickly close a running faucet.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 (New plumbing\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 has\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 "trapped\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 air\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 shock\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 absorbers"\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 to\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 reduce\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 this\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 effect.)\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Decelerating\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 column of\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 water\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 pipes\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 by\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 closing\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 valve causes a sharp pressure rise that literally "rattle the pipes".\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This is the same situation as when the intake valve closes.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb3\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri821\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Inertia tuning is responsible for an increase in volumetric efficiency and torque over a broad RPM range.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Figure A.4.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 Inertia tuning is optimum\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 when the rise in intake runner pressure is\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 high over a broad range of the valve opening period, especially\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 around intake valve closing.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This usually occurs when In Tune Prs is highest in the RPM data test results.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 See Example 4.5.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb6\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\sl240\slmult1\f1\fs28\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Intake\expnd-2\expndtw-11  \expnd0\expndtw0 Resonance\expnd-2\expndtw-11  \expnd0\expndtw-2 Tuning\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li359\ri821\sl244\slmult1\sb236\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 Once the intake valve has closed, this pressure pulsation continues to be\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 reflected back and forth in the intake runner until the intake valve opens and the process starts again.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 If a high pressure peak of this reflected wave is at the intake valve during valve overlap, it can blow the burnt exhaust gasses out of the clearance volume into the exhaust.\expnd8\expndtw40  \expnd0\expndtw0 This results in additional gains in volumetric \expnd0\expndtw-2 efficiency.\par\sect\sectd\sbkpage\headery365\footery595\margtsxn740\margbsxn840\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\sb115\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\li360\ri799\sl244\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\expnd0\expndtw0\charscalex100 However, if a vacuum peak arrives at the intake valve during overlap, additional exhaust gasses will be drawn into the intake runner. This\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 process\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 hurts\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 volumetric\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 efficiency\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 since\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 cylinder\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 must\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 first\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 draw\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 in that\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 "blown\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 back"\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 exhaust\expnd0\expndtw-2  \expnd0\expndtw0 from\expnd-1\expndtw-3  \expnd0\expndtw0 the\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 intake\expnd0\expndtw-1  \expnd0\expndtw0 runner before it starts to induct the fresh, power producing air charge.\expnd13\expndtw64  \expnd0\expndtw0 The timing of this reflected wave to aid scavenging is called resonance \expnd0\expndtw-2 tuning.\par\pard\plain\s1\nooverflow\nocwrap\lnbrkrule\sl240\slmult1\f0\fs20\b0\i0\par
